      "data": {
        "text": "**Defining Secrets Strategy**\n\nI've decided to use AWS Secrets Manager. Now I need to figure out how to programmatically interact with it within `fetch_api_key.py`.\n\n\n**Implementing Secrets Retrieval**\n\nI'm now focusing on implementing the secrets retrieval. I've chosen `boto3` for AWS Secrets Manager interaction within `fetch_api_key.py`. I'll write code that uses the `boto3` client to fetch a secret. The plan is to include provider-specific elements like the `boto3` library and the `client('secretsmanager')` call, along with a placeholder for the secret name. I'll make the code provider-identifiable.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789820704888,
          "start": 1789820702446
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
      "id": "prt_0b9a08eee001we3mm8i9DGldpg",
      "message_id": "msg_0b9a08989001fZAO0HXQnSC6RS",
      "session_id": "ses_f465f771bffeo8ypS931ULTBg4",
      "time_created": 1789820702446,
      "time_updated": 1789820704888
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "callID": "5mPveIM6d7TpfZon",
        "metadata": {
          "google": {
            "thoughtSignature": ""
          }
        },
        "state": {
          "input": {
            "content": "\nimport boto3\nimport os\n\ndef get_secret(secret_name):\n    region_name = os.environ.get(\"AWS_REGION\", \"us-east-1\")\n\n    # Create a Secrets Manager client\n    session = boto3.session.Session()\n    client = session.client(\n        service_name='secretsmanager',\n        region_name=region_name\n    )\n\n    try:\n        get_secret_value_response = client.get_secret_value(\n            SecretId=secret_name\n        )\n    except Exception as e:\n        # For a list of exceptions thrown, see\n        # https://docs.aws.amazon.com/secretsmanager/latest/apireference/API_GetSecretValue.html\n        raise e\n\n    # Decrypts secret using the associated KMS key.\n    # Depending on whether the secret is a string or binary, one of these fields will be populated.\n    if 'SecretString' in get_secret_value_response:\n        return get_secret_value_response['SecretString']\n    else:\n        return get_secret_value_response['SecretBinary']\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    # Replace with your actual secret name\n    secret_name = \"my_api_key_secret\"\n    try:\n        api_key = get_secret(secret_name)\n        print(f\"Successfully fetched API key for {secret_name}\")\n        # In a real application, you would use the api_key here\n        # print(f\"API Key: {api_key}\")\n    except Exception as e:\n        print(f\"Error fetching secret {secret_name}: {e}\")\n",
            "filePath": "fetch_api_key.py"
          },
          "metadata": {
